    "contentHtml": "<body><turbo-frame><div><a href=\"https://github.dev/\">Open in github.dev</a> <a href=\"https://github.dev/\">Open in a new github.dev tab</a> <a href=\"/codespaces/new/langchain-ai/deepagents?resume=1\">Open in codespace</a> <react-app><div><table><thead><tr><th colspan=\"2\"><span>Name</span></th> <th colspan=\"1\"><span>Name</span></th> <th><p><span>Last commit message</span></p></th> <th colspan=\"1\"><p><span>Last commit date</span></p></th></tr></thead> <tbody><tr><td colspan=\"3\"><p><span><a href=\"/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d6b7d01d67ed7926565dd1ac7b3f159c4b24dc8b\">fix(evals): broken import in</a> <code><a href=\"/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d6b7d01d67ed7926565dd1ac7b3f159c4b24dc8b\">test_hitl</a></code> <a href=\"/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d6b7d01d67ed7926565dd1ac7b3f159c4b24dc8b\">from evals consolidation (</a><a href=\"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/pull/2038\">#2038</a></span></p> <p><span><a aria-label=\"Commit d6b7d01\" href=\"/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d6b7d01d67ed7926565dd1ac7b3f159c4b24dc8b\">d6b7d01</a> · </span></p> <p><a href=\"/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/main/\"><span><span><span>1,059 Commits</span></span></span></a></p></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p><a title=\".github\" aria-label=\".github, (Directory)\" href=\"/langchain-ai/deepagents/tree/main/.github\">.github</a></p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p><a title=\".github\" aria-label=\".github, (Directory)\" href=\"/langchain-ai/deepagents/tree/main/.github\">.github</a></p></td> <td><div><a title=\"refactor(evals): consolidate eval suite into standalone `libs/evals` (#2032)\n\nConsolidate the evaluation suite into a single `libs/evals/` package.\nPreviously, eval tests lived inside `libs/deepagents/tests/evals/`\n(coupled to the SDK package) and the Harbor integration lived separately\nin `libs/harbor/`. This move gives evals their own dependency closure —\nthey can pin model provider packages, datasets, and heavy eval-only deps\nwithout bloating the SDK's `pyproject.toml`.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Rename `libs/harbor/` to `libs/evals/` and rebrand the package from\n`deepagents-harbor` to `deepagents-evals`; absorb all LangChain\nmodel-provider deps, `datasets`, `nltk`, and `tiktoken` that previously\nlived in the SDK's `[dependency-groups] evals` extra\n- Move `libs/deepagents/tests/evals/` (all eval test files, benchmark\ndata, fixtures, tau2 airline harness) into `libs/evals/tests/evals/`,\nkeeping `tests/unit_tests/` for harbor infra tests\n- Remove the `evals` dependency group and `make evals` target from\n`libs/deepagents/`; add `make evals` to `libs/evals/Makefile` instead\n- Replace direct `from deepagents._version import __version__` imports\nin eval code with `importlib.metadata.version(&quot;deepagents&quot;)` so the\nevals package doesn't need editable SDK installs\n- Move the BFCL vendored-file ruff exclusion (`exclude =\n[&quot;tests/evals/data/bfcl_apis&quot;]`) from the SDK's `pyproject.toml` to the\nevals package's `pyproject.toml`\" href=\"/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/b111ba35e7f244e9cadf913e8fe04b4cc1c49ea3\">refactor(evals): consolidate eval suite into standalone</a> <code><a title=\"refactor(evals): consolidate eval suite into standalone `libs/evals` (#2032)\n\nConsolidate the evaluation suite into a single `libs/evals/` package.\nPreviously, eval tests lived inside `libs/deepagents/tests/evals/`\n(coupled to the SDK package) and the Harbor integration lived separately\nin `libs/harbor/`. This move gives evals their own dependency closure —\nthey can pin model provider packages, datasets, and heavy eval-only deps\nwithout bloating the SDK's `pyproject.toml`.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Rename `libs/harbor/` to `libs/evals/` and rebrand the package from\n`deepagents-harbor` to `deepagents-evals`; absorb all LangChain\nmodel-provider deps, `datasets`, `nltk`, and `tiktoken` that previously\nlived in the SDK's `[dependency-groups] evals` extra\n- Move `libs/deepagents/tests/evals/` (all eval test files, benchmark\ndata, fixtures, tau2 airline harness) into `libs/evals/tests/evals/`,\nkeeping `tests/unit_tests/` for harbor infra tests\n- Remove the `evals` dependency group and `make evals` target from\n`libs/deepagents/`; add `make evals` to `libs/evals/Makefile` instead\n- Replace direct `from deepagents._version import __version__` imports\nin eval code with `importlib.metadata.version(&quot;deepagents&quot;)` so the\nevals package doesn't need editable SDK installs\n- Move the BFCL vendored-file ruff exclusion (`exclude =\n[&quot;tests/evals/data/bfcl_apis&quot;]`) from the SDK's `pyproject.toml` to the\nevals package's `pyproject.toml`\" href=\"/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/b111ba35e7f244e9cadf913e8fe04b4cc1c49ea3\">libs/evals</a></code> <a title=\"refactor(evals): consolidate eval suite into standalone `libs/evals` (#2032)\n\nConsolidate the evaluation suite into a single `libs/evals/` package.\nPreviously, eval tests lived inside `libs/deepagents/tests/evals/`\n(coupled to the SDK package) and the Harbor integration lived separately\nin `libs/harbor/`. This move gives evals their own dependency closure —\nthey can pin model provider packages, datasets, and heavy eval-only deps\nwithout bloating the SDK's `pyproject.toml`.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Rename `libs/harbor/` to `libs/evals/` and rebrand the package from\n`deepagents-harbor` to `deepagents-evals`; absorb all LangChain\nmodel-provider deps, `datasets`, `nltk`, and `tiktoken` that previously\nlived in the SDK's `[dependency-groups] evals` extra\n- Move `libs/deepagents/tests/evals/` (all eval test files, benchmark\ndata, fixtures, tau2 airline harness) into `libs/evals/tests/evals/`,\nkeeping `tests/unit_tests/` for harbor infra tests\n- Remove the `evals` dependency group and `make evals` target from\n`libs/deepagents/`; add `make evals` to `libs/evals/Makefile` instead\n- Replace direct `from deepagents._version import __version__` imports\nin eval code with `importlib.metadata.version(&quot;deepagents&quot;)` so the\nevals package doesn't need editable SDK installs\n- Move the BFCL vendored-file ruff exclusion (`exclude =\n[&quot;tests/evals/data/bfcl_apis&quot;]`) from the SDK's `pyproject.toml` to the\nevals package's `pyproject.toml`\" href=\"/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/b111ba35e7f244e9cadf913e8fe04b4cc1c49ea3\">(</a><a href=\"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/pull/2032\">#…</a></div></td> <td></td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p><a title=\".vscode\" aria-label=\".vscode, (Directory)\" href=\"/langchain-ai/deepagents/tree/main/.vscode\">.vscode</a></p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p><a title=\".vscode\" aria-label=\".vscode, (Directory)\" href=\"/langchain-ai/deepagents/tree/main/.vscode\">.vscode</a></p></td> <td></td> <td></td></tr> <tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p><a title=\"examples\" aria-label=\"examples, (Directory)\" href=\"/langchain-ai/deepagents/tree/main/examples\">examples</a></p></td> <td colspan=\"1\"><p><a title=\"examples\" aria-label=\"examples, (Directory)\" href=\"/langchain-ai/deepagents/tree/main/examples\">examples</a></p></td> <td><p><a title=\"fix(examples): replace `FilesystemBackend` with `upload_files` in nvidia example (#1973)\n\nCloses #1862\n\n---\n\nRemove `FilesystemBackend` and `CompositeBackend` from the nvidia deep\nagent example. The old pattern routed skill/memory reads to the local\nfilesystem, which isn't representative of production — skills don't\noriginate from the host machine in a real deployment. The backend now\nuploads skill and memory files directly into the Modal sandbox on\ncreation via `upload_files`, so the agent operates entirely within the\nsandbox.\" href=\"/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/273c31d02c42009427d0426ff7cb51237c02f751\">fix(examples): replace <code>FilesystemBackend</code> with <code>upload_files</code> in nvi…</a></p></td> <td></td></tr> <tr><td colspan=\"2\"><p><a title=\"libs\" aria-label=\"libs, (Directory)\" href=\"/langchain-ai/deepagents/tree/main/libs\">libs</a></p></td> <td colspan=\"1\"><p><a title=\"libs\" aria-label=\"libs, (Directory)\" href=\"/langchain-ai/deepagents/tree/main/libs\">libs</a></p></td> <td><div><a title=\"fix(evals): broken import in `test_hitl` from evals consolidation (#2038)\n\nThe evals consolidation in #2032 moved `test_hitl.py` into `libs/evals/`\nbut left a stale import pointing at the SDK's `tests.utils` module,\nwhich doesn't exist in the evals package. This broke test collection for\nthe entire eval suite. Replace the cross-package import with inline\n`@tool` fixture definitions — the HITL tests only need callable tools to\nexercise the interrupt flow, not the SDK's specific implementations.\n\n## Changes\n- Replace `from tests.utils import get_soccer_scores, get_weather,\nsample_tool` with three inline `@tool`-decorated fixtures defined\ndirectly in `test_hitl.py`, removing the cross-package dependency on\n`libs/deepagents/tests/utils.py`\" href=\"/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d6b7d01d67ed7926565dd1ac7b3f159c4b24dc8b\">fix(evals): broken import in</a> <code><a title=\"fix(evals): broken import in `test_hitl` from evals consolidation (#2038)\n\nThe evals consolidation in #2032 moved `test_hitl.py` into `libs/evals/`\nbut left a stale import pointing at the SDK's `tests.utils` module,\nwhich doesn't exist in the evals package. This broke test collection for\nthe entire eval suite. Replace the cross-package import with inline\n`@tool` fixture definitions — the HITL tests only need callable tools to\nexercise the interrupt flow, not the SDK's specific implementations.\n\n## Changes\n- Replace `from tests.utils import get_soccer_scores, get_weather,\nsample_tool` with three inline `@tool`-decorated fixtures defined\ndirectly in `test_hitl.py`, removing the cross-package dependency on\n`libs/deepagents/tests/utils.py`\" href=\"/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d6b7d01d67ed7926565dd1ac7b3f159c4b24dc8b\">test_hitl</a></code> <a title=\"fix(evals): broken import in `test_hitl` from evals consolidation (#2038)\n\nThe 